FIX FE "View League" trap (832): season/standings setups stored raw &LAB_00453c00 as a fn-ptr

QA agent Finding: on the between-race Championship standings screen ("Relegated", scr168),
pressing Enter on the "View League" icon threw `table index is out of bounds` (and once escalated
to a renderer crash). Root = the same runtime-fn-ptr-store class as patch 824, but a form 824
missed: End_Of_Season / the @0x46af78 standings-menu setups (FUN_00454318/4543a8/454438/4544c8/
454558) / Display_Season_Status / FUN_004558ec store `PTR_LAB_0046af90 = &LAB_00453c00` (and
`PTR_LAB_0046c07c = &LAB_00453c00`). LAB_00453c00 = `(*(undefined4*)GIMG(0x453c00))`, so
`&LAB_00453c00` = the RAW VA 0x453c00 -- not the relocated table index. dd2_relocate rewrites the
STATIC slot at boot, but these setups RE-STORE the raw VA at runtime, so the later call_indirect
of [0x46af90]/[0x46c07c] (the "View League" viewer FUN_00453c00) traps OOB. In championship
(race_type!=3) the else-branch always takes this path. Patch 824 only fixed the LITERAL
`= 0x453c00` store in the reconstructed FUN_004545e8; these 8 pre-existing `&LAB_` stores were
missed. Fixed all 8 to store the relocated `FUN_00453c00` (matching the working `= View_MultiLeague`
sibling line). The View_MultiLeague (race_type==3) branch was already correct.

verify + verify-wasm 10/10 both; native<->wasm L9 702/702 bit-identical.
